        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/23019147?u=4c0de81596ced64dc067dea5686f7ca2912db0cb&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This PR primarily adds the \"Brief history of hash-based SPA routing\" section to the <a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Glossary/Router\" rel=\"nofollow\">Router</a> glossary page.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Other changes are minor edits for formatting, punctuation, and clarity on the \"Router\" and <a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/History_API/Working_with_the_History_API\" rel=\"nofollow\">Working with the History API</a> pages.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">We were missing historical context for hash routing. The new section informs developers why <code class=\"notranslate\">#/</code> and <code class=\"notranslate\">#!/</code> routing practices came about, why they are obsolete now, and what to use instead.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">/cc <a class=\"user-mention notranslate\" data-hovercard-type=\"user\" data-hovercard-url=\"/users/tantek/hovercard\" data-octo-click=\"hovercard-link-click\" data-octo-dimensions=\"link_type:self\" href=\"https://github.com/tantek\">@tantek</a></p>",
