        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47647?u=2fbfc431a85d357f00c0146d5e55b425b7f00a3d&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Chrome 136+ supports the <a href=\"https://w3c.github.io/mediacapture-surface-control/\" rel=\"nofollow\">Captured Surface Control</a> API, another extension to the <a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Screen_Capture_API\" rel=\"nofollow\">Screen Capture API</a>. See <a href=\"https://chromestatus.com/feature/5092615678066688\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://chromestatus.com/feature/5092615678066688</a> for details of the addition.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This PR documents the new features, providing reference docs and a guide.</p>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h3>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Additional details</h3>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Related issues and pull requests</h3>\n\n\n\n",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/39982",
            "title": "Document the Captured Surface Control API",
            "date_modified": "2025-06-20T17:53:25.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-06-18T14:09:52.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "chrisdavidmills",
                "url": "https://github.com/chrisdavidmills"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47647?u=2fbfc431a85d357f00c0146d5e55b425b7f00a3d&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Chrome 136+ supports the <code class=\"notranslate\">MediaTrackSettings.screenPixelRatio</code> property, on desktop only. See <a href=\"https://chromestatus.com/feature/6738236535472128\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://chromestatus.com/feature/6738236535472128</a> for details.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This PR adds a ref page for the new property.</p>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h3>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Additional details</h3>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Related issues and pull requests</h3>\n\n\n\n",
